## 10. Explanation of Dimensions and Facts

### Dimensions

| Dimension | Business Question Supported | Main Attributes |
|---|---|---|
| DimDate | What are the hiring trends over time? | `date_id`, `year`, `month`, `day` |
| DimTechnology | Which technical profiles generate the highest number of hired candidates? | `technology_key`, `technology_name` |
| DimSeniority | Which candidates generate the highest number of hires, by professional seniority? | `seniority_key`, `seniority_level` |
| DimCountry | What differences exist between geographic regions? | `country_key`, `country_name` |
| DimCandidate | What hiring trends and proportions exist by estimated gender? | `candidate_key`, `first_name`, `last_name`, `email`, `estimated_gender` |

### Facts (FactApplication)

| Measure | Meaning | Source / Calculation |
|---|---|---|
| code_challenge_score | Candidate's technical performance in the code challenge | Source data |
| technical_interview_score | Candidate's technical performance in the interview | Source data |
| yoe | Numeric value representing the candidate's years of experience | Source data |
| is_hired | Determines whether the candidate is hired or not | `code_challenge_score ≥ 7 AND technical_interview_score ≥ 7` |
| score_gap | Difference between the candidate's two evaluation scores | `code_challenge_score − technical_interview_score` |
| cantidad_candidatos | Count measure to identify the number of candidates who applied | `SUM(cantidad_candidatos)` |
| cantidad_contrataciones | Count measure to identify the number of hires made | `SUM(cantidad_contrataciones)` |
| proporcion_contratados | Measure evaluating the hiring proportion | `cantidad_contrataciones / cantidad_candidatos` |

## 11. ETL Architecture

![Arquitectura ETL](./diagrams/pipeline-etl.png)


## 12. Main Transformation Decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|---|---|
| Application Date as String to DateTime | Standardize date format for proper time-series analysis and dimensional aggregation |
| Gender Estimation (UNKNOWN) | All candidates marked as UNKNOWN due to Genderize API rate limitations; structure supports future gender data enrichment |
| IS_HIRED Business Rule | Implemented as `code_challenge_score ≥ 7 AND technical_interview_score ≥ 7` for consistent hiring classification |
| Slowly Changing Dimensions (SCD) | Dimension tables implement SCD Type 1 (overwrite) since candidate attributes are assumed stable |
| Additive Facts | All measures in FactApplication are additive, allowing direct aggregation across dimensions |
| Surrogate Keys | Auto-increment INT keys on all dimensions for efficient FK relationships |
| Score Gap Calculation | Pre-calculated in ETL (`code_challenge_score - technical_interview_score`) to support evaluation gap analysis |
| Duplicate Records Handling | INSERT IGNORE used to prevent duplicate dimension entries while loading fact table |

